## **The Problem:**

Your `functions.php` only loads:
```html
<link rel='stylesheet' id='abundant-thought-2025-v5-0-style-css' href='https://abundantthought.com/2025/wp-content/themes/abundant-thought-2025-v5-0/style.css?ver=5.0' media='all' />
```

But **NOT** `assets/css/theme.css` where the menu styling is located.

## **Immediate Fix:**

You need to **update your `functions.php`** to enqueue BOTH CSS files. Replace your current enqueue function with this:

```php
/**
 * Enqueue scripts and styles for the front end
 */
function abundant_thought_2025_v5_0_scripts() {
    // Main theme CSS (with menu styling) - LOAD THIS FIRST
    wp_enqueue_style(
        'abundant-thought-2025-v5-0-theme',
        get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/css/theme.css',
        array(),
        '5.0'
    );

    // Theme metadata stylesheet (style.css) - LOAD SECOND
    wp_enqueue_style(
        'abundant-thought-2025-v5-0-style',
        get_stylesheet_uri(),
        array('abundant-thought-2025-v5-0-theme'), // Depends on theme.css
        '5.0'
    );

    // Theme JS (if present)
    if ( file_exists( get_template_directory() . '/assets/js/theme.js' ) ) {
        wp_enqueue_script(
            'abundant-thought-2025-v5-0-scripts',
            get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/js/theme.js',
            array( 'jquery' ),
            '5.0',
            true
        );
    }

    // Comments support
    if ( is_singular() && comments_open() && get_option( 'thread_comments' ) ) {
        wp_enqueue_script( 'comment-reply' );
    }
}
add_action( 'wp_enqueue_scripts', 'abundant_thought_2025_v5_0_scripts' );
