### 💡 Recommended Implementation Approach

For the custom post types, I strongly recommend the **plugin approach** rather than keeping them in your theme[citation:1]. This follows WordPress best practices because:

- **Updates won't break your site** - Theme updates won't affect your custom content types
- **Content remains portable** - You can change themes without losing post type functionality
- **Better separation of concerns** - Theme handles presentation, plugin handles content structure

The CSS fixes ensure your theme will properly display WordPress-generated content like image captions, aligned elements, and gallery items[citation:2][citation:7].

