**2. If NOT set up, here's how to do it once:**

**In `tailwind.config.js`:**
```javascript
module.exports = {
  content: ['./index.html', './src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx}'],
  theme: {
    extend: {
      fontFamily: {
        // Set Trebuchet as default sans font
        sans: [
          '"Trebuchet MS"', 
          '"Segoe UI"', 
          'Roboto', 
          'Helvetica Neue', 
          'Arial', 
          'sans-serif'
        ],
      },
    },
  },
  plugins: [],
}
```

**3. OR in your main CSS file (index.css or App.css):**
```css
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Trebuchet+MS:wght@300;400;700&display=swap');

@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

@layer base {
  html {
    font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
}
```

**4. OR as a fallback using system font (no web font load):**
Since Trebuchet MS comes with Windows/Mac, you can use the system version:
```css
@layer base {
  html {
    font-family: "Trebuchet MS", "Segoe UI", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
  }
}
```

